<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  MAGENTO'S OWN SIGN-IN POPUP IS REMOVED. SPARTRAK ALREADY REPLACED IT.
  ===========================================================================
  Magento_Customer's default.xml mounts `authentication-popup` into the
  `content` container of EVERY frontend page - a Knockout component rendering
  the "Checkout using your account / Checkout as a new customer" box.

  Nothing on this storefront shows it. Spartrak has its own auth modal
  (Magento_Theme/layout/default.xml -> `spartrak.auth_modal`, template
  html/login-modal.phtml, widget web/js/spartrak-auth.js), it is mounted on
  every page by the same default handle, and web/js/spartrak-auth-popup-mixin.js
  wraps `Magento_Customer/js/model/authentication-popup::showModal` so that the
  minicart, the cart page and Magento_Checkout's own sign-in link all open the
  SPARTRAK modal instead. Core's popup was reachable only through that mixin's
  fallback branch, which cannot fire while the Spartrak modal is on the page.

  So it was rendering, and booting, purely to be ignored.

  ===========================================================================
  WHAT IT COSTS TO KEEP - MEASURED, NOT ESTIMATED
  ===========================================================================
  The block is cheap; its JavaScript is not. Magento_Customer/js/view/
  authentication-popup declares:

      'Magento_Ui/js/form/form'   -> which itself requires 'mage/validation'
      'mage/validation'           -> 'jquery/validate', 'jquery/metadata',
                                     'Magento_Ui/js/lib/validation/rules'
      'Magento_Ui/js/lib/validation/rules' -> 'moment'

  Read off the homepage's own Lighthouse script treemap (decoded bytes, and
  the share of each file Chrome reported as never executed):

      moment.min.js                  58,912 B   74% unused
      mage/validation.min.js         42,412 B   71% unused
      jquery/jquery.validate.min.js  32,881 B   89% unused
      Magento_Ui .../validation/rules ~26,819 B
      jquery/jquery.metadata.min.js   1,542 B   78% unused
      Magento_Ui/js/form/form.min.js  4,131 B   66% unused
      + action/login, modal/alert, Security/js/escaper, the three captcha
        components other modules attach to this block, its messages child,
        and one XHR for authentication-popup.html
      =============================================================
      roughly 170KB decoded and ~15 requests, on every page

  Spartrak's own modal asks for none of it: spartrak-auth.js declares jquery,
  mage/translate, Magento_Customer/js/customer-data, mage/cookies and
  jquery/ui-modules/widget, and its forms carry `novalidate` and validate
  themselves. That is the whole reason this removal is possible.

  NOT CLAIMED: the jQuery UI dialog tree (dialog, draggable, resizable,
  position, effects, jquery-color - about 145KB) does NOT go away. It arrives
  through Magento_Ui/js/modal/modal, which Magento_Ui/js/modal/confirm still
  needs for the minicart's remove-item confirmation. Same reasoning as the note
  in Magento_Ui/web/js/lib/knockout/bindings/bootstrap.js.

  ===========================================================================
  WHAT ELSE POINTED AT THIS BLOCK
  ===========================================================================
  Five other layouts add CHILDREN to it - Magento_Captcha, Magento_Checkout,
  Magento_Persistent (remember_me), Magento_ReCaptchaCustomer and
  Smartwave_Dailydeals. They go with it, which is correct: they were decorating
  a popup that never opened. Magento skips a <referenceBlock> whose target has
  been removed rather than failing, so nothing here needs a matching edit.

  Removing the popup does NOT remove a sign-in route. Checkout's own
  `Magento_Checkout/js/view/authentication` sign-in link calls showModal() and
  therefore lands on the Spartrak modal via the mixin, and guests never reach
  checkout at all - Spartrak\Checkout\Plugin\PromptLoginForGuest redirects them
  to the cart with #auth=login first.

  The mixin's fallback branch was updated in the same change: with core's markup
  gone, "no Spartrak modal here" now navigates to customer/account/login instead
  of calling a popup that has no DOM. See spartrak-auth-popup-mixin.js.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="authentication-popup" remove="true"/>
    </body>
</page>
